  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "To help quell some of the anger about the loss of mods but also just because it would be a nice thing to have, why not have some sort of official plugin system or steam workshop support. This would put moderation control into VRC's hands, while making sure that \"modding\" itself is actually improved, since this would probably entail some sort of plugin framework provided by the SDK. EAC can remain, and people get the option to make custom add-ons back, now safer and easier than ever. Overall this would be a win-win.\nThe only issue with this that is obvious to me right now is the large development time attached to something like this, and the problem of moderating these plugins properly, so this is very much a suggestion for further down the line, though there are probably some solutions to \"community authorised\" plugins, similar to how worlds sit in an unauthorised state at first.",
